data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":", the scent of sandalwood incense drifts from ancient wooden temples, the rhythmic click of *geta* (wooden sandals)","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" echoes on cobblestone streets, and the seasonal beauty of nature is treated with a reverence found nowhere else on earth.\n\n","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"This guide will help you navigate the timeless elegance of Kyoto, from its iconic shrines to its hidden culinary gems.\n\n##","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" When to Visit: The Dance of the Seasons\n\nKyoto is a city defined by its seasons. To visit Kyoto is","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" to witness a changing masterpiece.\n\n*   **Spring (Late March – Early April):** This is the season of","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" *Sakura* (cherry blossoms). The city turns into a soft cloud of pink and white. It is undeniably beautiful","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":", but be prepared for significant crowds and higher hotel prices.\n*   **Autumn (November):** Many travelers argue","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" that autumn is even more spectacular than spring. The maple trees (*momiji*) turn brilliant shades of crimson and gold,","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" framing the dark wood of temples in a fiery glow.\n*   **Summer (June – August):** Kyoto summers","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" are famously hot and humid. However, this is the season of the Gion Matsuri, one of Japan’s","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" most famous festivals, featuring massive, ornate floats.\n*   **Winter (December – February):** If you seek","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" solitude, winter is your season. A light dusting of snow on the Golden Pavilion is a sight of ethereal beauty, and","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" the crowds are at their thinnest.\n\n## Essential Districts and Landmarks\n\n### 1. Higashiyama: The","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" Living Museum\nWalking through the Higashiyama district feels like stepping into a woodblock print. The sloping streets of **","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"Sannenzaka and Ninenzaka** are lined with traditional wooden buildings, tea houses, and artisan shops. ","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"\n\nAt the crown of this district sits **Kiyomizu-dera**, a massive wooden temple built without a single","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" nail. The view from its large veranda, overlooking the city framed by cherry or maple trees, is legendary. As you","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" descend, stop at small shops to try *yatsuhashi* (cinnamon-flavored rice flour sweets), a","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" local specialty.\n\n### 2. Arashiyama: Nature’s Grandeur\nOn the western outskirts lies Ar","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"ashiyama, a district defined by its relationship with the mountains and the river. The **Sagano Bamboo Forest** is","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" a must-visit; walking through the towering, swaying green stalks provides a sensory experience unlike any other. Nearby, the","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

